Hi,

I'm Emily Whitaker, senior buyer at Spring Garden Tools Ltd — a UK
gardening accessories brand stocked in approximately 200 independent
garden centres and three national DIY chains across England, Scotland,
and Wales. I'm writing to request a quote for our spring 2027 stock-up
window.

Product specification:

- Stainless steel hand trowel, full-tang construction (blade and handle
  core forged as one piece), hardwood handle (ash or beech, your
  choice, but please confirm wood type in your quote)
- 28 cm overall length, polished SS304 blade approx. 6 cm wide at the
  widest point
- CE marking for the EU market — we still sell into the Republic of
  Ireland and our retailer there requires EU compliance
- BSCI compliance from the factory — Tesco (one of our big channel
  partners) asks for this annually

Quantity: 8,000 units

Target FOB price: USD 2.30 per unit

Packaging: Each trowel in a clear plastic sleeve with a branded header
card at the top (we'll supply the artwork — single-colour print on
white card). 24 trowels per inner carton, 4 inner cartons per master
carton (96 units / master carton).

Customisation: Our "Spring Garden Tools" logo and the text "Made in
China for UK Distribution" laser-engraved on the blade — one position,
roughly 3 cm × 1 cm. We accept a one-off tooling fee up to USD 200; if
you require more please flag in your quote.

Payment terms: 30% deposit at PO confirmation, 70% against B/L copy
once the goods are on the vessel.

Shipping: Sea freight, FOB Shanghai. Our forwarder is OEC (HK office)
— they'll handle the booking from Shanghai once we know the carton
dimensions, total CBM, and gross weight.

Critical timeline — please read carefully:

We are working against a hard retail-calendar deadline.

- We will issue PO on 22 March 2027 (deposit will be wired same day,
  so funds reach you 23-24 March).
- Please plan approximately 30 days of production from deposit
  received.
- Sea freight from Shanghai to Felixstowe (UK port) typically takes
  about 30 days transit in our experience — your freight estimate may
  vary slightly depending on the carrier and routing.
- Goods must arrive at our Northampton distribution centre by
  15 April 2027 so we can re-pack and ship out to retailers ahead of
  the Easter weekend (16-17 April 2027). Easter is our single biggest
  selling weekend of the year, accounting for approximately 40% of Q2
  revenue. Missing the Easter window means the entire stock becomes
  off-season inventory we'd have to discount heavily.

Please send your detailed quote (cost breakdown by line: FOB unit
price, tooling, sample fee, packaging, certification) by
5 February 2027.

If the timeline above looks tight given your production and lead-time
realities, please tell me honestly — we have some flexibility on order
quantity (could drop to 5,000-6,000 if needed) but the Easter dates
are hard. I'd much rather hear the truth now than find out in late
March that we're going to miss the window.

